# 01. Phase 06 Scope & Objectives

## 01.1 Objective

Phase 06 establishes the frontend system from which every GrowFlow surface can be consistently implemented.

The intended outcome is:

> Any approved Phase 01 page can be implemented without inventing a new visual language, shell, state model, API access pattern, permission pattern, or interaction pattern.

## 01.2 In Scope

- frontend architecture
- frontend project structure
- design system implementation
- shared component system
- application shell
- role-aware navigation
- authentication presentation
- authorization-aware UI
- state architecture
- API integration
- SSE integration
- AI UX
- project workspace patterns
- responsive behavior
- accessibility
- performance
- testing
- observability
- Stitch workflow
- page implementation governance

## 01.3 Out of Scope

This phase does not:

- redefine the product
- replace frozen routes
- replace backend architecture
- replace canonical domain rules
- silently add product features
- implement all pages
- make Stitch the source of truth
- permit frontend-only business rules to become canonical

## 01.4 Success Condition

Phase 06 succeeds when the frontend is a coherent system rather than a collection of independent screens.

## 01.5 Primary Principle

**Foundation before page production.**

