# 02. Frontend Technology Architecture

## 02.1 Architecture Model

The frontend follows:

```text
Application
    ↓
Routing / Guards / Providers
    ↓
Page / Route Layer
    ↓
Feature Layer
    ↓
Domain UI Layer
    ↓
Shared Component Layer
    ↓
State / Data Layer
    ↓
API / Realtime Layer
    ↓
FastAPI Backend
```

## 02.2 Presentation Layer

Owns:

- visual composition
- rendering
- interaction wiring
- accessibility presentation
- responsive composition

Does not own canonical business state.

## 02.3 Route/Page Layer

Owns:

- route composition
- page-level data requirements
- route parameters
- page loading/error boundaries
- page-specific composition

## 02.4 Feature Layer

Owns domain workflows such as:

- projects
- assessments
- blueprints
- tasks
- milestones
- risks
- documents
- GitHub
- AI
- groups
- students
- mentors
- administration

## 02.5 Domain UI Layer

Represents reusable domain concepts.

Examples:

- ProjectHeader
- TaskRow
- MilestoneSummary
- RiskIndicator
- BlueprintStatus
- AIExecutionStatus
- DocumentVersion
- ActivityItem

## 02.6 Shared Component Layer

Contains generic UI primitives and reusable patterns.

Shared components must not contain hidden product-specific business rules.

## 02.7 Data Layer

Provides:

- API access
- request orchestration
- response normalization where required
- server-state caching
- mutation handling
- invalidation/reconciliation

## 02.8 Realtime Layer

Owns:

- SSE connection lifecycle
- event validation
- subscription management
- reconnection
- event deduplication
- canonical reconciliation

## 02.9 Technology Selection Boundary

Framework/library choices may be selected for implementation, but must preserve the architecture and contracts in this document.

A technology choice is not permission to change the domain architecture.

