# 04. Design Tokens

## 04.1 Token Layers

```text
Primitive Tokens
    ↓
Semantic Tokens
    ↓
Component Tokens
    ↓
Page Composition
```

## 04.2 Primitive Tokens

Include:

- color primitives
- spacing
- typography
- radii
- borders
- shadows
- breakpoints
- motion durations
- opacity
- z-index

## 04.3 Semantic Tokens

Examples:

```text
background-primary
background-secondary
surface
surface-muted
text-primary
text-secondary
text-tertiary
border-subtle
border-default
accent
success
warning
danger
info
ai-surface
ai-border
```

## 04.4 Component Tokens

Components may expose semantic variants through component-level tokens.

## 04.5 Token Consumption Rule

Page code should consume semantic/component tokens rather than scattering raw values.

## 04.6 Token Extension Rule

A new token requires a real reusable need.

Do not create near-duplicate tokens for individual pages.

