# 05. Typography & Content System

## 05.1 Typeface Direction

Use a Manrope-style geometric humanist sans consistent with Phase 03.

## 05.2 Hierarchy

Provide clear levels for:

- display
- page title
- section title
- subsection title
- body
- supporting text
- metadata
- labels
- table content
- code
- AI output

## 05.3 Typography Rules

Avoid:

- excessive weights
- giant headings without purpose
- unreadably small metadata
- inconsistent line height
- arbitrary type scales

## 05.4 Content Hierarchy

Visual hierarchy should communicate:

1. identity
2. context
3. primary task
4. important state
5. supporting information
6. secondary actions

## 05.5 Text Constraints

Long content must be handled through:

- wrapping
- truncation where safe
- expansion
- tooltips where appropriate
- detail views

Important information must not disappear solely because of truncation.

