# 13. AI / Streaming UX Foundation

## 13.1 AI Philosophy

AI is embedded intelligence, not a separate visual universe.

## 13.2 AI Visual Direction

Use a slightly deeper Soft Intelligence variant.

Avoid:

- neon
- glow overload
- animated particles
- fake typing
- artificial certainty

## 13.3 AI Execution States

```text
QUEUED
 ↓
RUNNING
 ↓
VALIDATING
 ↓
QA
 ↓
COMPLETED
```

Failure branches:

```text
FAILED
CANCELLED
RETRYING
```

## 13.4 AI Progress

Only show progress that corresponds to meaningful backend execution information.

Do not fabricate percentages.

## 13.5 AI Results

Where appropriate, show:

- execution status
- stage
- result
- validation
- QA
- timestamps
- errors
- retry status
- related resource

## 13.6 AI Mentor

AI Mentor is contextual to the project.

Context can include:

- project
- blueprint
- tasks
- milestones
- risks
- documents
- activity

## 13.7 AI Output

AI output is untrusted until validated by backend processes.

## 13.8 Streaming Architecture

```text
Persistent Backend Job
        ↓
Persistent Event
        ↓
SSE
        ↓
Streaming State
        ↓
UI
        ↓
Canonical Reconciliation
```

## 13.9 SSE Lifecycle

```text
Connect
 ↓
Authenticate
 ↓
Subscribe
 ↓
Receive Event
 ↓
Validate
 ↓
Update Streaming State
 ↓
Reconcile Server State
```

## 13.10 Reconnection

Support:

- disconnect detection
- reconnection
- missed-event recovery
- duplicate protection
- canonical refetch

## 13.11 SSE Is Not Canonical

SSE is a delivery mechanism only.

## 13.12 Browser Independence

Long-running AI work must continue even if the browser closes or navigates away.

## 13.13 AI Failure

Failure must remain visible and recoverable.

