# 15. Frontend ↔ Backend Integration

## 15.1 Canonical Flow

```text
UI
 ↓
Feature/Data Layer
 ↓
API Client
 ↓
FastAPI
 ↓
Application Services
 ↓
Domain Services
 ↓
Canonical State / External Systems
```

## 15.2 API Boundary

Components must not scatter raw network calls.

## 15.3 API Contract

Each integration defines:

- endpoint
- method
- request
- response
- auth
- permission
- errors
- loading
- mutation behavior

## 15.4 Server State

Includes:

- fetched resources
- canonical backend data
- cache
- mutation results

## 15.5 UI State

Includes:

- modal
- drawer
- filters
- tabs
- expanded rows
- temporary form state
- sidebar state

## 15.6 Streaming State

Includes:

- execution progress
- live events
- processing
- connection status
- reconnection status

## 15.7 State Separation

Do not maintain competing copies of canonical domain truth.

## 15.8 Cache

Caching is derived and must not become a new source of truth.

## 15.9 Reconciliation

After relevant mutations or streamed events, reconcile with authoritative server state.

## 15.10 Error Mapping

API errors must map to appropriate UX states without hiding their meaning.

## 15.11 Authentication Flow

```text
