# 16. Security, Accessibility, Performance & Testing

## 16.1 Frontend Security

Never expose:

- provider API keys
- service-role secrets
- privileged credentials
- private integration secrets

## 16.2 Security Boundary

Frontend controls presentation.

Backend controls authorization.

## 16.3 Admin

No impersonation unless separately and explicitly designed.

Inspection is not impersonation.

## 16.4 Sensitive Data

Minimize sensitive data in:

- client state
- logs
- URLs
- analytics
- error reports

## 16.5 AI Content

Sanitize untrusted AI/Markdown output.

## 16.6 Accessibility

Shared components must establish:

- semantic HTML
- labels
- accessible names
- focus behavior
- keyboard interaction
- contrast
- screen-reader behavior

## 16.7 Keyboard

Critical workflows must be keyboard usable.

## 16.8 Focus

Dialogs/drawers must:

1. move focus appropriately
2. constrain interaction appropriately
3. restore focus on close

## 16.9 Reduced Motion

Respect user reduced-motion preferences.

## 16.10 Motion

Default motion follows Phase 03:

> Float → Settle

Motion must communicate physical continuity rather than decoration.

## 16.11 Performance

Priorities:

1. initial load
2. route transitions
3. large data
4. images
5. charts
6. documents
7. AI UI
8. SSE
9. mobile

## 16.12 Code Splitting

Public pages should not unnecessarily load heavy authenticated/admin modules.

## 16.13 Image Optimization

Use:

- responsive sizing
- lazy loading where appropriate
- optimized assets

## 16.14 Large Data

Use:

- pagination
- virtualization where needed
- incremental loading
- efficient rendering

## 16.15 SSE Performance

Prevent:

- duplicate subscriptions
- unnecessary reconnect loops
- excessive rerenders
- abandoned connections

## 16.16 Testing Pyramid

```text
Unit
 ↓
Component
 ↓
Integration
 ↓
E2E
```

## 16.17 Unit

Test deterministic utilities, validation, formatting, state transformations, and permission helpers.

## 16.18 Component

Test:

- rendering
- interactions
- states
- accessibility

## 16.19 Integration

Test:

- API
- auth
- permissions
- server state
- mutations
- SSE reconciliation

## 16.20 E2E

Critical workflows include:

- registration
- login
- onboarding
- project selection
- project creation
- assessment
- blueprint generation
- tasks
- milestones
- project changes
- mentor supervision
- admin investigation

## 16.21 Visual Regression

Recommended targets:

- shell
- public pages
- dashboard
- project workspace
- AI
- tables
- documents
- dark theme
- mobile

