# 18. Phase 06 Implementation Rules & Freeze

## 18.1 Rule: One Design System

GrowFlow has one design system.

## 18.2 Rule: One Shell

GrowFlow uses one shell architecture.

## 18.3 Rule: One Canonical State

Backend/domain state remains authoritative.

## 18.4 Rule: No Direct Database Access

Frontend never accesses the canonical database directly.

## 18.5 Rule: No Direct AI Provider Access

Frontend never calls AI providers directly.

## 18.6 Rule: No Secret Leakage

Secrets remain server-side.

## 18.7 Rule: No Silent Mutation

UI must not silently alter canonical state through assumptions.

## 18.8 Rule: No Silent Definition Mutation

Changing a Project Definition must not silently mutate existing instances.

## 18.9 Rule: No Browser-Dependent Jobs

Long-running work survives browser navigation.

## 18.10 Rule: SSE Is Delivery

SSE never becomes the sole source of truth.

## 18.11 Rule: No Fake AI State

AI UI must reflect real execution state.

## 18.12 Rule: No Fake Progress

Do not invent execution percentages.

## 18.13 Rule: No Unauthorized Actions

A hidden button is not security. Backend authorization is mandatory.

## 18.14 Rule: Accessibility

New components and pages must be accessible.

## 18.15 Rule: Responsive

New pages must define desktop, tablet, and mobile behavior.

## 18.16 Rule: Architecture Changes

Architecture changes require:

```text
Discover
 ↓
Document
 ↓
Evaluate
 ↓
Approve
 ↓
Update Authority
 ↓
Implement
```

## 18.17 Rule: Component Reuse

Prefer reuse and composition.

## 18.18 Rule: Page Contract

Every page must satisfy the Phase 04 page implementation contract.

## 18.19 Rule: Error Completeness

Every major page/workflow must define loading, empty, error, success, and relevant processing states.

## 18.20 Rule: Traceability

Every implementation must be traceable to the applicable frozen specification.

